From a92a40780b1f543a4ada89dff3b1c2169978a329 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Theorem Labs
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:12:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [compiler-rt] sealed init: the last two unchecked raw mmap
 returns

Patch 0016 caught the raw -errno at ReservedAddressRange::Init, which is where
it could reach InitAligned's fixup and the secondary's CHECK(p).  Two more
callers consume an unchecked raw return, and this closes them so that the claim
about mechanism (C) is a claim about ALL of it rather than about the consumers
someone found.

The enumeration, from the patched tree.  Every caller of MmapNoAccess and
MmapFixedNoAccess on Linux:

  ReservedAddressRange::Init          raw, and 0016 guards it
  MapDynamicShadow                   raw, UNGUARDED  <- this patch
  MapDynamicShadowAndAliases         raw, UNGUARDED  <- this patch
  ProtectGap (x2)                    compares res against addr -> checked
  tsan  MemoryRangeIsAvailable       compares against beg    -> checked
  msan  ProtectMemoryRange (x2)      compares against beg    -> checked
  dfsan (x2)                         compares against beg    -> checked

So the unchecked set has exactly three members and 0016 covered one.  Everything
else that takes one of these two functions' results compares it against the
address it asked for, which detects a -errno implicitly.

MapDynamicShadow has the identical defect to Init's, not merely a similar one:
MmapNoAccess returns (uptr)-errno, the CHECK_NE below it rejects only exactly
-1, so every other errno passes, the RoundUpTo wraps, and what comes out is
UnmapFromTo's "(to >= from) != 0" with an empty stack and no mention of memory
or mmap.  That message is already known here -- toolchain/Dockerfile's
build-time check had to learn to accept it as a second spelling of "could not
reserve the shadow".

NEITHER IS REACHABLE IN A SEALED ASan BINARY, and that is deliberate rather than
an oversight to hunt for: FindDynamicShadowStart returns kSealedShadowOffset
before it gets to MapDynamicShadow, which is what pinning the riscv64 offset was
for, and MapDynamicShadowAndAliases is hwasan's alone.  They are converted on
0015's own stated rule -- the shadow-interleave abort in asan_shadow_setup.cpp
was guarded on exactly this basis, "held to the same rule so that it is not an
exception waiting to become one".  A reviewer should not look for a reachable
path; there isn't one today, and the point is that the rule does not depend on
that staying true.

Written with inline internal_iserror to match 0016 rather than introducing a
helper.  Nothing changes in an unsealed binary, and nothing changes in a sealed
one either, since neither site is reached -- the guard inventory goes from
eleven to thirteen and the observable behaviour of every binary this project
builds is unchanged.
---
 .../sanitizer_common/sanitizer_linux_libcdep.cpp   | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_linux_libcdep.cpp b/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_linux_libcdep.cpp
index 794fbf1a0..8ea6a5ee4 100644
--- a/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_linux_libcdep.cpp
+++ b/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_linux_libcdep.cpp
@@ -1126,6 +1126,16 @@ uptr MapDynamicShadow(uptr shadow_size_bytes, uptr shadow_scale,
   const uptr map_size = shadow_size + left_padding + alignment;
 
   const uptr map_start = (uptr)MmapNoAccess(map_size);
+  // The same unchecked raw return as ReservedAddressRange::Init's, and the same
+  // reason the CHECK below does not catch it: MmapNoAccess hands back
+  // (uptr)-errno and CHECK_NE rejects only exactly -1, so every other errno
+  // passes, the RoundUpTo wraps, and the failure surfaces as UnmapFromTo's
+  // "(to >= from) != 0" with no mention of memory.  Unreachable in a sealed
+  // ASan binary -- FindDynamicShadowStart answers kSealedShadowOffset before it
+  // gets here -- and held to the rule anyway, the way the shadow-interleave
+  // abort is.  See SealedHangOnAllocationFailure.
+  if (UNLIKELY(internal_iserror(map_start)))
+    SealedHangOnAllocationFailure();
   CHECK_NE(map_start, ~(uptr)0);
 
   const uptr shadow_start = RoundUpTo(map_start + left_padding, alignment);
@@ -1184,6 +1194,10 @@ uptr MapDynamicShadowAndAliases(uptr shadow_size, uptr alias_size,
   const uptr map_size = left_padding + 2 * alignment;
 
   const uptr map_start = reinterpret_cast<uptr>(MmapNoAccess(map_size));
+  // The last unchecked raw return in the tree; hwasan's, and no ASan binary
+  // reaches it.  See SealedHangOnAllocationFailure.
+  if (UNLIKELY(internal_iserror(map_start)))
+    SealedHangOnAllocationFailure();
   CHECK_NE(map_start, static_cast<uptr>(-1));
   const uptr right_start = RoundUpTo(map_start + left_padding, alignment);
 
